{"type":"thinking","text":"Now I can decode the HUD. Columns 2-9 rows 3-6 are 0xF5 = minimap (gray). Column 10 blank, 11 = border.\n\nRow 3 (first counter line): x=12: 0x21, x=13: 0x01, x=14: 0x01 → I bet 0x21 = \"X\", 0x01 = digit \"1\". So \"X11\" = rupee count 11. Then x=15..20: 0x69, 0x0B, 0x6B, 0x69, 0x0A, 0x6B, and row 4 x=15,17,18,20 = 0x6C. So x=15..20 is a 2×? region: it's actually the B item box? Wait 0x69/0x6B corners and 0x6C edges? Hmm.\n\nActually the Zelda HUD has, right of the minimap: three rows of counters, each formatted \"[icon][X][tens][ones]\"? Row 3: X11 (rupees). Row 5: x=12:0x21, x=13:0x0A → \"X\" + \"0\"?? Hmm x=13=0x0A. Row 5: 0x21, 0x0A → \"X\" and something. Row 6: x=11:0x61, x=12:0x21, x=13:0x07.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider: Row 3: x11=0xF7 (icon?), x12=0x21 (\"X\"), x13=0x01, x14=0x01 → \"X11\"? But where's the rupee icon? 0xF7 at x11 could be the rupee icon.\nRow 5: x11=0xF9 (icon?), x12=0x21 (\"X\"), x13=0x0A → \"X\" + one digit. 0x0A = \"0\"? Hmm, maybe 0x0A is digit \"0\" and 0x01 is \"1\". So \"X0\" = 0 bombs? But screenshot seemed to show X6.\nRow 6: x11=0x61 (icon?), x12=0x21 (\"X\"), x13=0x07 → \"X7\"? Hmm 0x07 = digit 7 → keys = 7? Hmm.\n\nWait row 6 x11=0x61 might be a key icon (0x61). Row 5 x11=0xF9 might be bomb icon. Row 3 x11=0xF7 rupee icon. Hmm but wait row 3 x12=0x21 \"X\", x13=0x01, x14=0x01 = \"11\" rupees. Row 5: x12=0x21, x13=0x0A... 0x0A is not \"0\"? In Zelda the digit tiles might be 0x00-0x09 where 0x00=\"0\". But 0x0A? Hmm. Actually maybe 0x01=\"1\" and 0x00=\"0\". Then 0x0A would be...? \n\nHmm wait, maybe digits are 0x0A-0x13? Let me read a digit tile. Let me read_tile 0x01 (CHR 1) and 0x0A (CHR 10). Since background pattern table is 0x1000, chr_tile = tile_id + 256. Earlier get_tile_at_pixel said background_pattern_addr 4096 (0x1000), and chr_tile for tile_id 247 was 503 = 247+256. So read_tile tile_id = nametable tile_id + 256.\n\nSo to see tile 0x21 = 33 → CHR 289. Let me read CHR 257 (tile 1), 266 (0x0A), 2