0x62.\n\nSo on row 3 we have: [0xF7] [X] [1] [1] then [0x69][0x0B][0x6B][0x69][A][0x6B] then \"LIFE\".\nHmm, [0x69][0x0B][0x6B] and [0x69][0x0A][0x6B] — these are box borders with contents: 0x0B and 0x0A inside. So the B box contains item tile 0x0B, and the A box contains item tile 0x0A = \"A\"?? no. Wait, the \"A\" at x=19 is tile 0x0A which we decoded as letter \"A\" — but that's in the A item box? Hmm, the A box in the screenshot is empty. Hmm.\n\nHmm wait, the boxes: In the screenshot, \"B\" box (2 tiles wide, with a dark item inside) and \"A\" box (empty). The tiles 0x69/0x6B are box corners; 0x0B and 0x0A are contents; 0x6B at x20 is box bottom-right; row 4 has 0x6C at x15,17,18,20 = box edges.\n\nActually the box structure: x15=0x69, x16=0x0B, x17=0x6B, x18=0x69, x19=0x0A, x20=0x6B. Plus row4 x15=0x6C,x17=0x6C,x18=0x6C,x20=0x6C. So each box is 3 tiles wide? x15-17 (top row) and x15,x17 row4 → a 3x2 box with the item at x16. Similarly x18-20. So B box item = 0x0B, A box item = 0x0A. Hmm, but if 0x0A=\"A\", maybe the A box shows the letter \"A\"? No—the item glyphs. Hmm, 0x0B might be a sword? Let me not care.\n\nWait, actually the boxes in Zelda HUD are drawn with tiles like 0x69 (top-left corner?), 0x6B, 0x6C... and the item tile inside. The \"A\" letter I decoded might actually be a sword/hud glyph coincidentally? Hmm, but the bitmap is clearly an \"A\".\n\nHmm hold on, maybe the \"B\" and \"A\" labels are at those positions: x=13,14 might be... no.\n\nLet me re-examine the screenshot: the HUD text: \"X11\" then \"B\" label then a box, then \"A\" label then a box, then \"-LIFE-\". Actually in the Zelda HUD, above the item boxes are the letters \"B\" and \"A\". Yes! The letters \"B\" and \"A\" appear above the boxes. So:\n- 0xB6? hmm.\n\nLet me map: x=13,14 = \"1\",\"1\" (rupees), x=15 = 0x69?, x=16=0x0B, x=17=0x6B... \n\nHmm, maybe the structure is: x13,14 = rupee digits; x15 = 0x69 (a tile?), x16 = 0x0B = letter \"B\"! (0x0B is likely \"B\"); x17=0x6B (top-