{"type":"thinking","text":"Watch results over 500 idle frames:\n- 0x66F: 6 → 5 at frame ~72 (took damage once), then stayed 5.\n- 0x670: 6 → 245 → 229 → 213 → 197 (decreasing by 16 every ~27 frames). Whoa! 0x670 is being overwritten by the game: 6→245→229→213→197. These values (245,214,197) decrease by 16. Hmm, 0x670 is being used by something else! So 0x670 is NOT max hearts — it's a scratch variable that the game overwrote.\n\nWait, but 0x670 baseline (after load) was 2. And now after 500 frames it's 245 etc. So 0x670 is volatile/scratch. So max hearts isn't 0x670.\n\nHmm, but the baseline read showed 0x66F=2, 0x670=2 and the display showed 1 heart. And 0x66F decreased to 5 after damage (from 6) → 0x66F IS current health! Confirmed: damage decreased it by 1 (half heart). And the display... let me check the hearts now.\n\nSo 0x66F = current health in half-hearts. When I set it to 6 and Link had max 1 heart (2 half), the game likely clamped? It stayed 6→5. Hmm, but max hearts should be 2 (1 heart). Setting health=6 > max is odd; the game let it be 6 then damage made 5.\n\nSo max hearts: the display would show max hearts = ? Baseline 2 half-hearts = 1 heart. Where is max stored? Not 0x670 (scratch). Maybe 0x66E=3? or 0x664=7? Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe max hearts is in a different location. Let me reconsider the read trace: it read 0x66F (1) and 0x670 (241) — at that time 0x670 was 241 (volatile). So 0x670 being read by the HUD might be for something else (or the read trace caught a scratch read).\n\nHmm. So where is max hearts (containers)? \n\nThe display: hearts drawn at row6 x22 onward. The number of hearts = max health/2. Baseline 1 heart. The tile ids: full F2, half 65, empty 66.\n\nSo I need to find max health. Candidates: 0x66E=3? If max half-hearts = 3 → 1.5 hearts, but display showed 1 heart. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the display shows ceil(health/2) hearts total and empty beyond? Baseline health=2 → 1 heart. If max=2 → 1 heart. Hmm.\n\nLet me examine: after the damage, health=5 (2.5 hearts). The display should show 3 hearts (2 full + 1 half) if max ≥ 3 hearts. But max is 1 heart (2 half). Hmm, so maybe the display shows max hearts = 1? Then health 5 would be weird.\n\nLet me just look at the current hearts display and read 0x66F.\n\nAlso, max hearts might be derived from a \"heart containers\" byte elsewhere, maybe 0x66E? Let me test 0x66E.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the trace: it read 0x66F and 0x670 with PCs 0x6D10 and 0x6D15 (adjacent). If 0x66F=health and 0x670=max, the HUD reads both. But 0x670 is volatile... unless the game uses 0x670 for max hearts AND something else overwrites it? That can't be.\n\nHmm, actually, look at 0x670's watched values: 6 (my write), then 245, 229, 213, 197. It changed at frame 81+ (right after damage at frame ~72). 245=0xF5, 229=0xE5, 213=0xD5, 197=0xC5. These differ by 0x10. Interesting pattern: 0xF5, 0xE5, 0xD5, 0xC5. Hmm, high nibble F,E,D,C decreasing; low nibble 5. This looks like a *palette animation* or a color fade! 0xF5,0xE5,... are NES color bytes? Actually palette entries in this range (0xC5-0xF5) are reds/browns. Hmm.\n\nActually 0x670 might be part of a palette buffer that the game rotates. The \"damage flash\" animation palette! When Link takes damage, the screen flashes red — palette animation. So 0x670 got used as scratch for the flash. That explains the values.\n\nSo 0x670 is NOT max hearts. The read of 0x670 in the HUD trace was coincidental/it's a shared scratch.\n\nSo where's max health? Let me look at the display now: read nametable row 6 and memory 0x664-0x672.\n\nGiven health 0x66F=5 and max=2 (1 heart) baseline, the game let health exceed max... The display after damage — let me see.\n\nHmm, maybe max hearts is stored in the SAVE data and only updated on heart-container pickup. Could be at 0x66E? Let me test 0x66E.\n\nActually, maybe the heart display uses 0x66F as health and a separate max at, e.g., 0x66E? Baseline 0x66E=3 → 1.5 hearts; display 1 heart. Hmm.\n\nLet me test: write 0x66E = 6 and 0x66F = 6, then cause damage, see display. If 0x66E is max, we'd get 3 hearts.\n\nAlternatively, maybe hearts are stored as \"health\" at 0x66F and \"max\" at 0x66F-related byte in the save area (0x66E). Let me test 0x66E.\n\nBut careful: 0x66E baseline 3, and it's adjacent to rupees (0x66D) and health (0x66F). Could be max hearts! In Zelda, max hearts starts at 3 (3 hearts) and health in half-hearts starts at 6. But here baseline 0x66F=2 (health=1 heart!). Hmm, so this save has 1 heart max? That's unusual (Link has 1 heart?). Well, maybe the save is weird/partial.\n\nHmm wait, maybe 0x66F isn't health in half-hearts but in *quarter* hearts? Baseline 2 → hmm.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider: the display baseline showed ONE full heart (F2). 0x66F=2. After damage 0x66F=5?? That INCREASED from 2 to 6 (my write) then 5. But baseline without my write was 2. So damage from 2 would give 1, not 5. My write set it to 6, so damage 6→5. OK.\n\nSo with max presumably 2 (1 heart), health 6 is \"over-full\" — the display would show...? Let me look.\n\nLet me read the nametable row6 now and memory.\n\nI think the key insight: 0x66F = health (half-hearts). I still need max hearts/containers.\n\nLet me search for max hearts via the read trace: the HUD routine reads 0x66F and something else. The trace showed reads of 0x66D, 0x66F, 0x670, 0x67D, 0x67E, 0x664. Since 0x670 is scratch, maybe max hearts is 0x670 but only when not clobbered? Hmm, unlikely.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually maybe the game DOES store max hearts at 0x670, and the values 245,229,... are actually the max hearts *display* being corrupted... no, 0x670 as max=245 would draw 122 hearts.\n\nHmm, but during those 500 frames, did the heart display change? Let me check the current screen.\n\nLet me read nametable row 6 x18-31 and memory 0x660-0x680.\n\nLet me also test 0x66E. Actually, let me look at the save data: rupee 0x66D, health 0x66F, and between them 0x66E=3. If 0x66E=max hearts in half-hearts → 1.5 hearts. Hmm.\n\nHmm, actually maybe the layout is: 0x66D rupees, 0x66E max hearts(containers), 0x66F health. And 0x66C bombs? 0x66B keys? But the ramp test wrote to 0x66C=1 (bombs?) and the HUD row5 didn't change... unless bombs display only redraws on event.\n\nHmm, let me check: baseline 0x66C=0, 0x66B=3. If bombs=0x66C=0 and keys=0x66B=3? But HUD row6 showed \"7\"... Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the counter rows 5/6 aren't bombs/keys — maybe I've been wrong. Let me look at the CURRENT screenshot after damage: the HUD shows \"X11\" (rupees) and the two rows. Let me read the nametable and memory now.\n\nLet me do: read_memory 0x660 len 48, read_nametable x=10,y=5,w=5,h=2, screenshot.\n\nThen decide.\n\nActually, the important realization: 0x66F=health confirmed by the watch (6→5 on damage). Good.\n\nNow let me find max hearts. Let me test 0x66E=6 & 0x66F=6 with damage. But first, let me check the current heart display to understand.\n\nLet me batch reads."}
