sta 0x0302,y ; dey ; bpl\n```\nCopies 0x29 bytes from 0x6C97 to 0x0302. That's the OAM/sprite buffer (0x0302?). Hmm, 0x0302 might be the sprite buffer. So this routine is the HUD sprite/nametable update.\n\nHmm, actually 0x6C97 is in SRAM too. This is a copied routine.\n\nAnyway — the key: 0x66F and 0x670 are health and max hearts. Let me disassemble 0x6E79 to confirm and understand encoding.\n\nLet me also find bombs/keys: the routine continues at 0x6D1C reading 0x066D, then presumably 0x066C (bombs) and 0x066E (keys?) — let me disassemble 0x6D1C onward. Earlier at 0x6D1C: `ldx #0x02; lda 0x066d`. Let me disassemble 0x6D1A-0x6D90.\n\nLet me do two disassembles: 0x6E60 (for hearts) and 0x6D1A (for counters).\n\nActually one call each. Let me do 0x6D1A length 80 and 0x6E60 length 96.\n\nLet me run both."}
