top with a shaft going down and teeth.\n- A rupee: a diamond/hexagon.\n\n0x61:\n```\nrow0: 333 22 333\nrow1: 3 222222 3\nrow2: 3 222222 3\nrow3: 333 22 333\nrow4: 333 22 333\nrow5: 333 22 333\nrow6: .333333.\nrow7: ..3333..\n```\nThis has a vertical band (2s) down the middle and 3s on the sides — looks like a key: round head at top with a vertical shaft? Hmm, or the letter \"R\"? Actually it could be the key icon (round top and a shaft).\n\n0xF9: complex diagonal shapes — could be a bomb with a fuse and sparkle, or a rupee with facets.\n\nHmm. Let me use a different approach: read the two icon tiles at 2x2. Actually the counters might use 2x2 icon tiles: row5 x11 and row6 x11 are single tiles though.\n\nHmm, wait, in the HUD, the icons might be one tile each. Let me just look at the screenshot rendered: the icon next to the row5 counter and row6 counter. In the screenshot, the row5 icon (next to \"XA\"/\"X55\") appeared orange-ish (rupee?) and row6 icon similar. Hard.\n\nLet me try the community RAM map after all... but the task says no reference. Hmm, but I can determine by gameplay if I can change one.\n\nIdea: In Zelda, bombs are used by pressing B if the bomb is assigned to B. The A button uses the sword. If Link has bombs, pressing B places a bomb and the bomb count decreases by 1. Let me test: with 0x66E=55 and 0x0658=99 currently (so I can see changes), press B for a bit and see which counter decreases. If neither, then the B item isn't a bomb.\n\nAlso, the \"B item\" is 0x0664? Hmm.\n\nLet me try: play_input [{buttons:[\"b\"],frames:120}] watching 0x66E, 0x658, 0x66D.\n\nActually, pressing B in Zelda uses the B item. Let me just try and watch.\n\nAlso, keys: no easy change.\n\nHmm, alternatively, I can determine which is which by the ICON in the nametable: read the icon tile bitmaps and compare to the known rupee icon (0xF7, which is next to rupees). The row5 icon 0xF9 and row6 icon 0x61. Let me read 0xF7, 0xF9, and 0x61, and look for which resembles a key v